## Interface: 16001
## Title: High Fidelity World Map - Forever Map Data
## Notes: Required map art for High Fidelity World Map: Forever. Contains the stitched high-resolution world and continent maps, plus the tile placement data for zone and cave maps. No settings or UI of its own; install High Fidelity World Map to use it.
## Author: HighFidelityWorldMap
## Version: @project-version@
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Map02
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1727004
## X-HFWM-Data-Build:

# The tiles under WorldMap\ (the world and continent maps, nothing else) are
# read by High Fidelity World Map through their file paths, so they are not
# listed here. What is loaded is the lookup data that describes them and the
# placement data for everything drawn from the game's own minimap tiles.
# FDIDMap.lua (generated; FileDataID -> tile path, plus the HD continent
# layouts) defines plain HFWMF_* globals that the core addon reads at load
# time, after this addon (it RequiredDeps on it). The X-HFWM-Data-Build
# line is stamped by CI (.github/scripts/stamp-mapdata-toc.sh) with the
# generator hash the art was built from; the same hash is stamped into
# FDIDMap.lua as HFWMF_DATA_BUILD. Left empty in the repository, which the core
# addon treats as a dev build.
# MinimapTiles.lua: where each of the client's minimap tiles sits on a zone
# map. CaveTiles.lua: the same for cave and mine floors.
FDIDMap.lua
MinimapTiles.lua
CaveTiles.lua

# Runtime bridge for HighFidelityWorldMap: if this addon is disabled, this
# file never loads, and the core addon can suppress bundled textures.
Bridge.lua
